# Docs notebook conventions

`app/notebooks/<id>.notebook.yaml` is the notebook. These are auto-discovered and
solved by `app/scripts/build-notebook-data.mjs` — they are **not** moneyjs pilot
templates, so the submodule's `compile:notebook-yaml` does not apply. Never edit
`moneyjs/` or the generated `app/src/data/`.

## Collapsible "[more]" panels

Each cell can carry a collapsible "[more]" explanation. Two sources feed them; if
both define the same cell id, **inline wins**.

**Inline (preferred — `sim` uses this).** Add a `more:` block scalar to the cell
body in the YAML. The moneyjs parser ignores the field; the build script reads it:

```yaml
  - chart:
      id: baseline-chart
      title: Baseline
      variables: [Y, YD]
      sourceRunCellId: baseline-run
      more: |
        Output `Y` converges to `Y* = Gd / theta = 100` ...
```

**Sidecar (legacy — `bmw`, `gl2-pc`, `io-pc`).** A separate `app/notebooks/<id>.md`
where each panel starts with a marker on its own line; text runs to the next marker:

```
<!-- more: <cellId> -->
```

In both cases `<cellId>` must match a cell `id` in the YAML (unknown ids are skipped
with a warning); one block per id, last wins.

## Rendering: no KaTeX

Panels render via `AssistantMarkdown` (no `remark-math`). Use backticks, not LaTeX:

- ✅ `` `Y = Cs + Gs` `` and `` `alpha1` ``
- ❌ `$Y = C_s + G_s$`
- Use `pow(b, e)`, never `^`, for exponentiation.

In **inline** `more:` panels, write italics as `_italic_`, not `*italic*`: the
notebook YAML dialect scans block scalars and rejects `*word`/`&word` tokens
(they look like aliases/anchors). `**bold**` and ` * ` (multiplication in
backticks) are fine. Sidecar `.md` files are unaffected.

## Cells & scenarios

- One wrapper key per cell (`markdown`/`matrix`/`run`/`chart`/`table`/…); no `type`.
- `chart`/`table` `variables` are bare model variable names, not expressions.
- Scenario runs start from the baseline's last-period state; shocks (`constant` or
  `series`) apply over `rangeInclusive` and target **externals** only. A `series`
  maps `values[period - start]`. For growth, drive an external with a geometric
  `series`.

## Validation

Run `pnpm build:data` (solves every notebook — watch for `unknown cell id` and
`failed to solve` warnings), then `pnpm test`. `pnpm typecheck` currently fails on
pre-existing submodule errors, so it is not a reliable gate for notebook changes.
